messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "AI tools and climate adaptation enter daily life at scale.",
      "detail": "Generative and decision-support AI become standard in offices, homes, and public services, while cities expand heat, flood, and wildfire defenses. Supply chains and energy systems continue a multi-year shift toward electrification and resilience."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "EVs and heat pumps capture major shares of new sales in many markets.",
      "detail": "Total cost of ownership tips in favor of electrified transport and heating in most regions. Grid operators accelerate transmission expansions and flexibility markets to manage variable renewables."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Global CO2 emissions peak and begin a sustained decline.",
      "detail": "Policy, technology, and finance align to retire unabated coal and cap new oil demand. Methane abatement and efficiency deliver quick wins while renewables dominate new capacity."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "A global pathogen surveillance network sharply reduces outbreak sizes.",
      "detail": "Wastewater monitoring, rapid sequencing, and AI-driven risk detection become standard. Vaccines and antivirals are designed and deployed in months rather than years."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Grid-scale storage and renewables provide the majority of new electricity additions.",
      "detail": "Battery, thermal, and hydrogen storage make high-renewable grids reliable. Long-distance HVDC links and digital controls smooth variability across regions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2037,
      "event": "A grid-connected fusion demonstrator delivers sustained power output.",
      "detail": "It proves scientific and engineering viability but remains expensive compared with mature renewables and fission. Investment continues toward commercial designs."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Global warming approaches about 1.8 C above preindustrial levels.",
      "detail": "Extreme heat, droughts, and floods intensify, prompting large-scale adaptation and relocation programs. Food systems diversify with climate-resilient crops and controlled-environment agriculture."
    },
    {
      "year": 2043,
      "event": "Robust AI oversight becomes standard across high-stakes applications.",
      "detail": "Auditing, red-teaming, and alignment protocols are mandated in healthcare, finance, critical infrastructure, and national security. Near-general assistants are ubiquitous but operate under strict guardrails."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Longevity therapies modestly extend healthy lifespan.",
      "detail": "Gene editing, senolytics, and personalized medicine reduce late-life morbidity. Population aging continues, shifting labor markets and pensions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Global population peaks near 9.7 billion and major economies reach net zero.",
      "detail": "Emissions fall rapidly in power and transport, with industry and aviation relying on electrification, hydrogen, and carbon management. Air quality improves markedly in many megacities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Alternative proteins and precision fermentation transform food systems.",
      "detail": "Land use pressure eases as cultured and fermented proteins outcompete for cost and ethics in many markets. Some marginal agricultural land begins rewilding."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Managed retreat from the highest-risk coasts accelerates.",
      "detail": "Insurance, zoning, and public investment shift toward relocation and nature-based defenses. New inland and elevated coastal districts are planned for multi-decade resilience."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "Permanent crewed lunar facilities support science and industry.",
      "detail": "Polar water extraction, power beaming, and tele-robotic mining enable a cis-lunar economy. The Moon serves as a testbed for closed-loop habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Carbon dioxide removal scales to several gigatons per year.",
      "detail": "A mix of reforestation, soil carbon, enhanced weathering, biochar, and engineered direct air capture is financed by carbon markets and public programs. Monitoring and verification systems mature."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Fusion supplies a small but growing share of global electricity.",
      "detail": "Niche deployments complement a grid dominated by renewables and advanced fission. Costs improve with standardized reactors and advanced materials."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Global warming stabilizes near 2.1-2.4 C with improved adaptation.",
      "detail": "Heatwaves and storms remain dangerous, but mortality falls due to infrastructure and early warning. Biodiversity corridors and protected areas enable partial ecosystem recovery."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "A lunar settlement reaches about a thousand permanent residents.",
      "detail": "Habitats host families, schools, and small businesses supported by in-situ resource use and frequent Earth-Moon transport. Medical and life-support advances reduce off-world living risks."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Global mean sea level rises roughly 0.5-1.0 meters relative to 2000.",
      "detail": "Major ports and deltas are reconfigured; some low-lying nations have largely relocated. Carbon removal offsets residual emissions as most sectors approach deep decarbonization."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Large interstate wars remain rare as deterrence and transparency improve.",
      "detail": "AI-enabled sensing, arms control, and crisis hotlines reduce miscalculation, though cyber operations and proxy conflicts persist. Peacekeeping and humanitarian response become faster and more automated."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Universal real-time translation dissolves most language barriers.",
      "detail": "Cultural diversity thrives while cross-cultural collaboration becomes routine. Education and governance systems adapt to ubiquitous personalized tutoring and civic deliberation platforms."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Atmospheric CO2 falls below 420 ppm as net-negative operations persist.",
      "detail": "Ocean heat and ice-sheet inertia keep sea levels rising for centuries, demanding ongoing adaptation. Restoration economies mature around wetlands, forests, and reefs."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Martian and orbital communities reach tens to hundreds of thousands combined.",
      "detail": "Autonomous industry, closed-loop life support, and frequent cargo windows sustain off-world populations. Governance experiments balance local autonomy with Earth coordination."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Coastal geographies are transformed by committed multi-meter sea-level rise.",
      "detail": "Even as emissions stay net negative, past heat uptake drives long-term change. Many historical cities persist inland or behind large-scale defenses; others transition to heritage sites or artificial islands."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Human augmentation and synthetic organs become routine.",
      "detail": "Bioelectronic interfaces, gene therapies, and regenerative medicine normalize disability reduction and performance restoration. Ethical frameworks focus on access and consent."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "A robust economy spans the inner solar system.",
      "detail": "Asteroid resources and orbital manufacturing supply high-value materials and energy. Mars, the Moon, and free-space habitats host stable multi-generational communities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Cultural and biological diversification deepens without full speciation.",
      "detail": "Populations embrace varied augmentations and environmental adaptations but maintain inter-fertility and shared legal personhood. Identity and governance evolve to accommodate plural forms of life."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Long-lived institutions steward knowledge through civilizational cycles.",
      "detail": "Archives, automated tutors, and cultural compacts reduce knowledge loss during regional downturns. Scientific and historical records remain widely accessible."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Large orbital habitats host millions and space-based solar is widespread.",
      "detail": "High-efficiency power beaming and in-space construction decouple some industry from planetary surfaces. Environmental footprints on Earth decline further."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Earth’s climate remains warm and managed; new ice ages are postponed.",
      "detail": "Anthropogenic CO2 trajectories and deliberate climate stewardship forestall glacial inception. Adaptation remains a permanent policy and engineering domain."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Multiple cultural cycles rise and fall without species collapse.",
      "detail": "Regions experience periods of integration and decentralization, but global knowledge networks prevent total systemic failure. Risk management and disaster response are institutionalized."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Sea level approaches a quasi-equilibrium for the prevailing temperature.",
      "detail": "Shorelines stabilize with a mix of engineered barriers, living coastlines, and extensive retreat. Global population is smaller, older, and healthier on average."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Interstellar probes return long-horizon data from nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Autonomous craft powered by advanced propulsion and AI conduct multi-millennial surveys. Human presence persists across the solar system with periodic expansions and consolidations."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Human forms span a wide range of genetic and cyber-biological integrations.",
      "detail": "Morphological freedom is culturally accepted, with legal frameworks protecting personhood across diverse embodiments. Shared norms maintain interoperability and rights."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Early Holocene coastlines lie underwater and become archeological frontiers.",
      "detail": "Submerged cities and artifacts are cataloged by robots and virtual reconstructions. Cultural heritage industries flourish across Earth and space."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity endures in varied forms with limited interstellar footholds.",
      "detail": "A few outposts or autonomous biospheres exist around nearby stars, but most people live in the solar system. The species remains technologically capable and risk-aware, without galaxy-spanning colonization."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity likely decarbonizes, adapts to a warmer world, and becomes a multi-planet, knowledge-preserving civilization with pervasive AI and biotechnology, while avoiding species-level collapse. Over millennia, societies cycle and diversify, sea levels reshape coasts, and limited interstellar steps emerge, but most life remains centered on the solar system."
}
